I played with this a little and discovered you get the same result with

qplot(1:10, 1:10) + labs(title = title)

The theme_title() call appears to be ignored, as I would have expected since plot.title is not an argument of labs(), but instead is one of the ... arguments that is evidently unevaluated. AFAICT thus far, trying to pass theme_title() into element_text() is a no-go. I haven't seen anything thus far indicating that one can pass a theme function to a specific theme element in the new system, but that doesn't mean it's impossible.

The text in the title object contains several \n sequences that are recognized in 0.9.2, so it indicates that the new version can handle multiline titles. Now if it can do the same with expressions that contain \n sequences, I'll really be impressed :)

Dennis

