It's the stat="identity" that's screwing things up for you. Try

ggplot(tst,aes(x,y))+geom_bar(aes(fill=z2),position="stack")

which correctly puts z at the bottom of the stacks.

Ben

On Tue, Sep 11, 2012 at 3:07 PM,  <adam.l...@pnc.com> wrote:
> Hi all,
>
> Had a question about stacking if anyone has time.
>
> Not sure if it's unique to factors with three levels, but was having
> difficulty arranging stacks in a bar plot in the order required.
>
> The following example shows that changing the orders of the factor impacts
> the color pattern, but not the position of the levels in the stack. On the
> other hand, using the diamonds dataset, I was able to make the desired
> adjustment, so it's unclear to me what's unique about my example.
>
